{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic","id":1558608,"title":"Garou and Static Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-02T22:25:25-08:00","id":1558608,"title":"Garou and Static Magic","content":"My Mage character who is a Kinfolk has a Werewolf Companion, I was wondering could my character arrange for for their Garou Cousin to learn Hedge Magic like Herblisim and Healing.<br /> <br /> the Garou is a Hominid-Theurge-Black Fury, I know she has the Herbalist Skill.<br /> <br /> My Mage characters Mother is a Blood Aunt to the Garou (so a Kinfolk herself) and was my Mage Characters Mentor in Hedge Magic before they Awakend so I could arrange a Mentor if my Life, Matter and Prime Spheres and my Library Background are not Suitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T22:49:22-08:00","id":1558610,"title":"","content":"Garou are not banned from learning Path magic, but it is generally rare and unclear how much is cultural, practical, and a limited capacity. PC Garou require a 7 point Merit to do this, (not all Fera do), but it's left up to the idea of being &quot;innate&quot; or something that could be trained over time. It mostly exists to keep reflect the rarity aspect (mechanically it's not at all worth it).<br /> <br /> Is there a particular reason why you want to go this route? A base-line Theurge has easy access to their own methods of both instant magical healing and creating minor herbal concoctions for practically (if not usually better) results at a tiny fraction of the investment. I could understand if you're not sticking strictly to WtA conceits for a mage PC's related NPCs, but it sounds like you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T01:28:57-08:00","id":1558612,"title":"","content":"Talking with my Storyteller she wants an excuse for my Werewolf companion to show up more ATM of three stories she has shown up 0 times, her first and last appearance was at the start of my Prelude, my Kinfolk Merit was more use dealing with the local Sept two stories ago.<br /> <br /> My Character currently lives in Oakland and studies at UC Berkley, the Companion lives at the SoH/Black Fury Commune where my character grew up in Oregon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T03:42:23-08:00","id":1558615,"title":"","content":"Unless your game involves a lot of magical travel... the fact that you PC and their companion NPC live that far apart feels like a bigger issue than anything else.<br /> <br /> If the question is, how lore-appropriate would it be for the cousin to come down to Oakland to hangout with your PC and study magic? The answer is not really. As I said, a Theurge has very little benefit in terms of practical skills to learn from such instead of just using their Gifts and Rites. It's even less likely if Path magic is already common enough in the extended family that it's likely that there are other Kinfolk in the Oregon commune that know it and could just teach it there.<br /> <br /> A big factor is that the Garou put a lot of social pressure on the Garou to stay part of Garou groups: pack and Sept specifically. Running off for a few hours to hang out of family across town is one thing, spending months away, or doing regular huge trips, or overusing the Moon Bridges, is a fast way to get the Elders pissy and the spirits to start revoking Renown. <br /> <br /> I feel like you and your ST might have written yourselves into a bit of a corner here and might need to retcon things unless there's more you haven't said yet that could address matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T17:31:49-08:00","id":1558626,"title":"","content":"According to 1997's World of Darkness: Sorcerer, the answer is &quot;No&quot;, one of the Changing Breeds cannot normally learn Sorcery (the exception being some Bastet though that is always subject to ST approval). The idea is that Sorcery is something only living humans are capable of, and the Garou (and other Fera) are only partially human and partially something else. It just doesn't work for them. They might do everything correctly, but it just doesn't produce any results.<br /> <br /> I would also add that even if they were capable of learning Sorcery, that a Mage does not know Sorcery, they know Sphere Magic. The two are not the same even if they sometimes produce the same results. Attempting to teach Sphere Magic to non-Awakened does not result in Sorcery, it results in nothing. Your character's mother obviously does know Sorcery and thus could potentially teach it, but the Garou will simply be incapable of performing it as explained above.<br /> <br /> So that is the canon answer as far as I can tell. Like all things, STs can decide otherwise. Other rulebooks that the one I consulted might also have changed things.<br /> <br /> It would probably be more appropriate for a Garou NPC to learn additional Gifts (like rare Gifts or perhaps Gifts unique to your ST's chronicle) that provide similar benefits to those paths, assuming your Mage knows Spirit Spheres, knows various spirits, and can introduce more spirits to that Garou that she may not be aware of. However, since the Garou in question is a Theurge, she probably already has the necessary skills and friends (sept members, pack totem, etc.) to already provide that knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T20:57:10-08:00","id":1558630,"title":"","content":"The Mage Was a Sorcerer working mostly with Herblisim and Healing, till they started playing with Alchemy, this gave them their &quot;Oho &lt;Censored&gt;!&quot; moment and they awakened.<br /> <br /> the Mage is mostly Life, Mater and Prime, but has picked up dots in Sprint and Mind, would like a couple of dots in Forces, but the big target ATM is getting ready for a Seeking.<br /> <br /> not an American but how far in Hours Travel is the Bay Area to Oregon Timber Country, is it a short 6-8 hour trip or are you talking a day and a bit or more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T01:30:52-08:00","id":1558633,"title":"","content":"&quot;Timber Country&quot; isn't really a specific place. But you're talking 8-10 hrs to get to major cities or towns that are based in the timber industry and likely more the farther west you're going, and easily 2 extra hours if you're going off the highways to get to some commune tucked in the middle of the forests where a community of Garou and Kinfolk can live in relative obscurity.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure why you think 6 to 8 hours is an inherently &quot;short&quot; trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T18:36:40-08:00","id":1558645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558626#post1558626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to 1997's World of Darkness: Sorcerer, the answer is &quot;No&quot;, one of the Changing Breeds cannot normally learn Sorcery (the exception being some Bastet though that is always subject to ST approval). The idea is that Sorcery is something only living humans are capable of, and the Garou (and other Fera) are only partially human and partially something else. It just doesn't work for them. They might do everything correctly, but it just doesn't produce any results.<br /> <br /> I .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The rest of books mentioning the topic that I know states otherwise. <br /> <br /> Both bastet and kitsune are mentionned as learning sorcery both in every changing breed guides and in their respective breed book (in W20, it is present as a merit for either of those). <br /> <br /> That and the uktena have a secret camp made solely of sorcerer gerou","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T21:52:05-08:00","id":1558649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558633#post1558633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Timber Country&quot; isn't really a specific place. But you're talking 8-10 hrs to get to major cities or towns that are based in the timber industry and likely more the farther west you're going, and easily 2 extra hours if you're going off the highways to get to some commune tucked in the middle of the forests where a community of Garou and Kinfolk can live in relative obscurity.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure why you think 6 to 8 hours is an inherently &quot;short&quot; trip.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm from Australia, though I live just outside the 3rd biggest city in my youth I'd travel four hours to get to a game play for six to eight Crash out on the Couch for a few hours then drive home to catch a bit of sleep before going to a more local game that afternoon. on top of that My Mothers Family run Sheep and Cattle Stations out west and for them to pop next door or in to &quot;town&quot; is 4-6hrs each way and to get to a proper town is 6-8 hours, so my sense of Scale can be a bit different to Euros or Nor-Arms.<br /> <br /> Edit: also I think the Story Teller put them that far away so I wouldn't just cast &quot;Werewolf Companion&quot; to solve every problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","user":"Clive Coursor","date":". 03-05-2026, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T22:27:47-08:00","id":1558651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558645#post1558645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest of books mentioning the topic that I know states otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not aware of any. Can you provide specifics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558645#post1558645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both bastet and kitsune are mentionned as learning sorcery both in every changing breed guides and in their respective breed book (in W20, it is present as a merit for either of those).</div> </div> </div> </div>I already mentioned the Bastet as an exception in the quote you cited. If the Kitsune are added to that, so be it. But those are exceptions, and they don't apply to the others as a general rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558645#post1558645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and the uktena have a secret camp made solely of sorcerer gerou</div> </div> </div> </div>Which camp is this? I'm not aware of any such camp.<br /> <br /> The Path Dancers camp is mentioned as having rituals and Gifts not known to other Uktena, but rituals and Gifts are normal for Garou even if some are exclusive to certain small groups. Those aren't Sorcery Paths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T22:59:21-08:00","id":1558652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clive Coursor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558649#post1558649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm from Australia, though I live just outside the 3rd biggest city in my youth I'd travel four hours to get to a game play for six to eight Crash out on the Couch for a few hours then drive home to catch a bit of sleep before going to a more local game that afternoon. on top of that My Mothers Family run Sheep and Cattle Stations out west and for them to pop next door or in to &quot;town&quot; is 4-6hrs each way and to get to a proper town is 6-8 hours, so my sense of Scale can be a bit different to Euros or Nor-Arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to remember that there's more than just scale. Infrastructure and geography play a big part of time to travel that doesn't always translate to things like the raw distances involved.<br /> <br /> In the US, major cities frequently have very bad traffic infrastructure for their current populations and it spills over into the major highways. Starting in a major urban area like Oakland can add 30 min to an hour to a trip just because you're leaving/arriving at a bad time of day. While I live in a very different part of the US: I took public transportation to get to high-school. Not the fasted option, but no traffic. I could drive to my school in 15 minutes if there was nobody else on the road... but morning traffic regularly bumped the drive to over an hour... and light rail let me do it in 25 minutes consistently. Big cities in the US are also generally very unwelcoming to the kind of vehicles you want if you're regularly driving from an agricultural/timber/etc. small town in for something. For whatever reason US folks are allergic to utes (I never quite understood that, they make way more sense for most US people than our huge pickups do), it means there can be all sorts of weird things like trying to park something that's great for driving around timber land while in the city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: also I think the Story Teller put them that far away so I wouldn't just cast &quot;Werewolf Companion&quot; to solve every problem. </div> </div> </div>I understand the instinct to do that, but it still feels like it's gone a bit overboard in this case. As you noted, it's gone from &quot;can't have a werewolf solve all my problems&quot; to, &quot;the werewolf might as well not be on my sheet.&quot; The Garou live pretty busy lives. There are dozens of narrative reasons a Garou can be stuck between their work for their Sept and wanting to help their Kin-mage cousin, and it's simple enough to use the Elders being disapproving of dodging Sept duties too frequently to keep things in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T23:32:55-08:00","id":1558654,"title":"","content":"The Character drives a WWII Surplus turned USPS Surplus Jeep that was a &quot;Project Car&quot; before my character got their hands on it, The Werewolf normally drives a late 60's erly 70's era Charger or rides a mid century Indian Scout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T11:36:30-08:00","id":1558665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558651#post1558651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which camp is this? I'm not aware of any such camp.<br /> <br /> The Path Dancers camp is mentioned as having rituals and Gifts not known to other Uktena, but rituals and Gifts are normal for Garou even if some are exclusive to certain small groups. Those aren't Sorcery Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>...It is the Path Dancers. The discussion of them in the Revised tribebook kind of glosses that over, but those aren't actual Gifts and rites the speaker is talking about.<br /> <br /> (I think the discussion of them using sorcery is in the 2nd edition tribebook. I seem to be having a difficult time locating it in other books, but their use of &quot;non-standard&quot; mystic arts is definitely noted on p504 of W20)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T13:50:31-08:00","id":1558667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clive Coursor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558654#post1558654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Character drives a WWII Surplus turned USPS Surplus Jeep that was a &quot;Project Car&quot; before my character got their hands on it, The Werewolf normally drives a late 60's erly 70's era Charger or rides a mid century Indian Scout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool? Not the most practical options for the situation... but this seems to be getting hung up on less important details. Ultimately you need to focus on a way (either in-game or as I said earlier just handwave with your ST) to get your Garou NPC &quot;closer&quot; to the action of the actual play of the game so she can matter. Car/bike models don't do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T21:57:24-08:00","id":1558674,"title":"","content":"Well the Jeep is mostly to potter around the Bay Area to take them to places BART can't.<br /> <br /> I did a Road trip in a Big Block (VH) Valiant Charger of the same vintage in the early 90's from Gladstone to Newcastle (a bit over 1300km) it was a good trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T13:35:29-08:00","id":1558687,"title":"","content":"Few years ago we had a player who wanted to play a 'mage' (although he didnt get the sphere system but i digress) so we went for a compromise were he had path magic and was a theurge. It worked fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T03:20:48-08:00","id":1558701,"title":"","content":"I agree with the others that learning Sorcery is not the best excuse to have the companion visit the character, although as of Revised Sorcerer supernaturals are no longer categorically excluded from learning Paths. I wouldn't have a problem with allowing it, especially if it is a Path like Herbalism that is Ritual use only.<br /> <br /> But since the main issue seems to be balanced access to a character resource, I would look for alternative explanations for the companion to stick around for a while. Awakened kinfolk tend to have a complicated relationship with their family, due to the mistrust of Garou society against Mages - they are a risk towards their caerns and are usually involved with outside groups. But at the same time, these frictions can create narrative opportunities.<br /> <br /> Is the sept aware of the character's status as a Mage, or is this something only known to close family? Is the Mage part of a Tradition or Craft? If so, a diplomatic mission between sept and the Mage's affiliation might be a viable excuse to send the companion over solo to facilitate this. Even if the 'diplomacy' amounts to delivering the message to stay the heck away from the sept's territory. Or maybe whatever the Mage is dealing with could spiral into a problem that affects the sept.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T04:00:42-08:00","id":1558702,"title":"","content":"The Mage is a Sister of Hippolyta, before Awakening she was a Hedge Wizard. the SoH and a Pack of Black Furies run a &quot;Commune&quot; called &quot;Widows Peek&quot; that controls a (private) Conservancy attached to the Commune between a National Park and a State Forrest. the Commune supports itself through Organic Produce, Artisanal Crafts, Woman's Only Wellness Retreat (and Refuge for Abuse Survivors) and carefully managed &quot;Constructive Harvesting&quot; (to ensure Bio-Diversity and Fire Management) of the Conservancy<br /> <br /> Widows Peek is older and likely larger than the near by &quot;Town&quot; (generous to call it a Hamlet) of Pine Ridge, this is in a out of the way county called Alastair County the County Seat and only real Town in the County is called &quot;Red Wood&quot;, I wouldn't say most of the County are Inbreeds but apart from Widows Peek and a select few families the local Geean Pool is shallow enough to not have a wading end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T12:03:42-08:00","id":1558706,"title":"","content":"OK... I could say a lot about that... but ultimately it seems like a distraction from what we're saying: the details don't inform how to solve the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T13:05:04-08:00","id":1558707,"title":"","content":"This is off topic from your presented question, but I do want to say that I like the mage in question having been a sorcerer previously. It's a good background element for displaying occult competence prior to Awakening that I think is surprisingly underrepresented in terms of actual games in comparison to its presence in the setting. As for the matter of the werewolf learning path magic, I think that the matter of utility is being overstated? Especially when it comes to something as personal as magico-religious practice, I don't think one can think of their motivations in purely pragmatic terms. It could be the garou just wants to do something that their Gifts and Rites cannot, even if the effects are vastly lesser in power. Would say that whatever tradition involved might also just appeal more to them theologically, but based on the description it sounds very much in garou territory generally, so I do not think that is the case (come to think of it, a kinfolk sorcerer who studies some form of magic foreign to their family for religious reasons is a neat idea, and provides some useful adventure seeds).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T13:24:47-08:00","id":1558708,"title":"","content":"for those not up on Mage the SoH are a mixed &quot;Tradition&quot; mostly Hedge Wizards whit a hand full of Mages, they are descended from the Amazons and practice Comunilism and Goddess Worship and have ancient links to the Furies that for all but a few communities are today all but lost. M20 though including them in the Core Book relays on you getting your hands on some 2e books for the full story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T13:28:49-08:00","id":1558709,"title":"","content":"The problem with the character desires thing is that it's an NPC. It doesn't get the same leeway PCs tend to by default to play around with the expectations of the setting. Said NPC was raised in a culture that perceives human magic (Path or Awakened) as a spiritual aberration. Being in a sub-group that's more tolerant of it than average doesn't mean it's seen in a positive light. Studying it enough to do things you can't do with Gifts and Rites (and the two Paths in question don't really offer that) is not some little side project where you spend an hour or a week toying with some incantations. It's dedicating years of study and deep practice to do party tricks using tools most of your peers consider &quot;dirty&quot; at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T04:40:39-07:00","id":1558726,"title":"","content":"It's a highly unorthodox arrangement, but with that background context sending a Garou to a Mage for studies makes at least more sense.<br /> <br /> I had to think of the Cult of Isis when I read it. In case you are unfamiliar, it is a sorcerous affiliation that has been running for ages and counts mortals, Changing Breeds, and Mages among its members. At least before V5/W5.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Isis has a clear task and a paradigm that supersedes those of the respective parent organizations of its members; a Garou would have to juggle responsibilities towards the Nation (and usually Sept and Pack) and for this reason is likely to keep membership in the Cult a secret - and of course because the differing paradigm would be viewed as heretical by the larger Garou society.<br /> If your commune similarly has a 'grand secret' or 'greater goal' that supersedes that of Nation and Craft, it can serve as an explanation to coordinate its members in a way that would be highly unusual for either organization.<br /> <br /> Basically: if you transfer the highest authority to the commune, you can easily handwave sending the companion to the character for whatever reason as long as it aligns with the commune's paradigm. The price of course would be hell of a stink if this ever leaks to the Nation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With all that said, the most obvious and easiest solution imo would be to simply move the companion's pack 'on business' closer to the character's locale. That way the ST can control her availability depending on the 'business'. It's pretty handwavy, but sometimes simple works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T15:22:53-07:00","id":1558732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558608-garou-and-static-magic?p=1558651#post1558651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not aware of any. Can you provide specifics?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I already mentioned the Bastet as an exception in the quote you cited. If the Kitsune are added to that, so be it. But those are exceptions, and they don't apply to the others as a general rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which camp is this? I'm not aware of any such camp.<br /> <br /> The Path Dancers camp is mentioned as having rituals and Gifts not known to other Uktena, but rituals and Gifts are normal for Garou even if some are exclusive to certain small groups. Those aren't Sorcery Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bastet and kits une are the rule, not the exception. The only reason they're specifically mentionned is that they have a culture of using hedge magic. <br /> <br /> As for did camp, the path dancers, they are using soercerey, it is mentioned in both 1st Ed and revised tribe books and IIRC in at least one layeer's guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T16:06:23-07:00","id":1558734,"title":"","content":"Do not really see why there is such a degree of aggression towards Clive's idea as it stands? Or at least a significant degree of emotional investment against allowing the character to have a relationship with an NPC that probably won't matter much overall. If something like this happened in my home group's games it probably would not have drawn much attention at all. Just feel like there is a disconnect between the perceived setting implausibility of garou learning hedge magic and the actual problems posed by it. Either way the character is going to be gimping themselves from spending XP on situational abilities that are vastly weaker than their werewolf ones (although arguably that is not a problem in the situation described given how the werewolf is an NPC). <br /> <br /> As for the teaching and commuting situation, the main problem is that they live out-of-state; I cannot really see the mage effectively teaching the werewolf unless visits are so frequent as to be disruptive to the daily life of the mage, or unless they just end up using wireless communications, in which case the garou will probably have to perform enough independent daily work that they might as well just be an independent study, in which case there's the question of why the mage is involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T18:37:53-07:00","id":1558740,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything close to &quot;agression&quot; in this thread at all... even if I think people are getting to focused in debating which rules on Garou learning Path magic to apply that it's distracting from the point of bring it up.<br /> <br /> Nobody has expressed anything against a Mage PC with a werewolf Companion (something they put points towards on their sheet) having a relationship with that character. The whole issue is that the current state of Clive's game is one where the circumstances are already preventing them having a relationship that matches the intent.<br /> <br /> The core problem that I see being expressed is that the totality of issues with a Garou learning Path magic makes the idea of one regularly traveling ~10hrs to go study it with their cousin so that they're more present in the cousin's story just doesn't make much sense. There's a simpler set of solutions: change the game state so the cousins are closer to each other all the time so the fact that they're family is already plenty of reason for them to spend time together and the Garou NPC to end up more involved in the story than is currently happening. This set of options includes a lot less &quot;narrative&quot; solutions like the initial idea tries to do, but tends to be a more simple way to solve the main issue (frequency of NPC showing up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T20:20:05-07:00","id":1558741,"title":"","content":"I guess that the way the problem of distance was being presented made it seem like it was the mage and garou teaching relationship with hedge magic that was the problem rather than just the distance itself. If no one has an issue with the latter, then yeah I can definitely agree that the commute is the main trouble with the situation. Even apart from the metagame problem of the ST wanting to involve the NPC in play more, it seems unrealistic for the werewolf to go with the mage as a mentor instead of someone closer or going the autodidact route.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity Clive, does your mage have access to teleportation magic of some sort? It doesn't sound like she'd be the type to have Correspondence, but having an artifact or a mage buddy could help if the local Sept and the Oregon one do not permit usage of their moon bridges for this (which is realistic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T22:07:05-07:00","id":1558742,"title":"","content":"ATM she has Life 2, Mater 2, Mind 1, Prime 2, Sprint 1. is trying to get Forces and take her Arete to 3, just starting her 4th story and has about 30 odd hrs of game play and just short of 5 weeks in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T15:07:58-07:00","id":1558758,"title":"","content":"Huh, alright, that is fair. Will say that given those spheres it definitely seems like she will be needing outside help for transportation. Maybe you can check her backgrounds to see if she has contacts or anything that could reasonably give her pull with other mages? Although if your ST is the one wanting the NPC to be more involved in the goings on of the game, they might just fiat a way to bring them over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T22:08:28-07:00","id":1558766,"title":"","content":"Since start of play the Mage has picked up some Contacts and an Ally in both the Bay Area Werewolf Sept and the Bay Area Akashics, but an Antagonist (and possibly Enemy) in the Bay Area Wu Long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T22:55:38-07:00","id":1558767,"title":"","content":"So.... why not just work with your ST to get your PC's cousin to move to the nearby Sept? That seems like the simple way to solve the prime issue, and if you already have Background dots representing building a good relationship with the local Garou the issue of, &quot;I cast werewolf,&quot; is a bit lowered because you already can try to point local Garou at problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T11:44:54-07:00","id":1558771,"title":"","content":"An Ally sounds like a good way to justify having acquired some sort of magical transportation for the purpose that you are speaking of. You should probably bring that up with your Storyteller and see if you can work something out. In any case, the basic idea is quite cool and I wish you luck with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}